 {:db/id "42347e15-642d-5b7d-9335-656a5b86cb76"
  :question/id #uuid "42347e15-642d-5b7d-9335-656a5b86cb76"
  :question/problem "Source question: Assignment item (1), handout p. 1.\n\nSuppose $A$ is a $7\\times9$ matrix with $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=2$. What is the dimension of the row space of $A$? Briefly justify your answer. Remember that an example is just an example; it does not cover every possibility.\n\n$\\dim\\operatorname{Row}(A)=$ {{dimension}}. Give the justification in the written response."
  :question/answer-fields ["67392bb2-fa70-5825-8b29-9187721102a7" "908db3cb-345d-50b6-9fb3-dcb809f93a2a"]
  :question/worked-solution "Use the nine columns for rank-nullity. The resulting rank is also the dimension of the row space; the seven rows give a consistent upper bound, not the initial rank-nullity total."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
