 {:db/id "f9feb8c1-74bd-5fbd-b7fa-a9e491921afd"
  :answer/id #uuid "f9feb8c1-74bd-5fbd-b7fa-a9e491921afd"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "Put the input vectors in the columns of $P$ and their images in the matching columns of $Q$:\n$$P=\\begin{pmatrix}1&-1&0\\\\1&0&-1\\\\-8&6&3\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad Q=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&6\\\\3&4&1\\\\1&1&-1\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nThe required equation is $AP=Q$. Since $\\det P=1$, the inputs form a basis and $A=QP^{-1}$. Here\n$$P^{-1}=\\begin{pmatrix}6&3&1\\\\5&3&1\\\\6&2&1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\nA=\\begin{pmatrix}52&21&9\\\\44&23&8\\\\5&4&1\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nChecking $AP=Q$ verifies all three prescribed images. For example, the first image is $(52+21-72,44+23-64,5+4-8)^T=(1,3,1)^T$."
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
