 {:db/id "63c34434-9673-51e5-9301-9cd70d084fdc"
  :answer/id #uuid "63c34434-9673-51e5-9301-9cd70d084fdc"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "In the variable order $x,y,z$, the coefficient rows are $(1,2,3)$ and $(-3,2,1)$. Thus\n$$T(\\mathbf x)=A\\mathbf x,\\qquad A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&3\\\\-3&2&1\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nFor arbitrary $\\mathbf u,\\mathbf v\\in\\mathbb R^3$ and $\\alpha,\\beta\\in\\mathbb R$,\n$$T(\\alpha\\mathbf u+\\beta\\mathbf v)=A(\\alpha\\mathbf u+\\beta\\mathbf v)=\\alpha A\\mathbf u+\\beta A\\mathbf v=\\alpha T(\\mathbf u)+\\beta T(\\mathbf v).$$\nThis proves linearity, including both additivity and homogeneity."
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
