 {:db/id "5402f38e-9495-519d-8e62-16c3b411d8bd"
  :question/id #uuid "5402f38e-9495-519d-8e62-16c3b411d8bd"
  :question/problem "**(a)** $T\\!\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\\\z\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}x+2y+3z\\\\2y-3x+z\\end{pmatrix}$.\n\nShow that $T$ is linear and determine $A$ such that $T(\\mathbf x)=A\\mathbf x$.\n\n$A=$ {{matrix}}. Give the linearity justification in the written response."
  :question/answer-fields ["c6c2dcb8-987b-5fe8-a130-1faa61b2bb23" "c8278d2c-9b4d-5b10-9cc1-63113e3af298"]
  :question/worked-solution "Reorder the second component as $-3x+2y+z$ before reading its coefficients. A $2\\times3$ matrix has three input components and two output components; distributivity proves linearity."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
