 {:db/id "58af6c35-6ff6-5ad6-81e4-0aeb5432df34"
  :answer/id #uuid "58af6c35-6ff6-5ad6-81e4-0aeb5432df34"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "Every linear map sends the zero vector to the zero vector, because $T(\\mathbf0)=T(0\\mathbf v)=0T(\\mathbf v)=\\mathbf0$. Here\n$$T\\!\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\0\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}\\ne\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nTherefore this $T$ is not linear. This single counterexample disproves a property that a linear map must satisfy for every input."
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
