  :question/id #uuid "9e570354-c90a-5b20-86e8-3b55efc5851b"
  :question/problem "Source question: Assignment item (5); Kuttler 2017A, Exercise 5.3.2, printed p. 285 (PDF p. 297).\n\nLet $T$ be the linear transformation induced by\n$$A=\\begin{pmatrix}3&1\\\\-1&2\\end{pmatrix},$$\nand let $S$ be the linear transformation induced by\n$$B=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-2\\\\4&2\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nFind the matrix of $S\\circ T$ and find $(S\\circ T)(\\mathbf x)$ for $\\mathbf x=\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}$. Show supporting work.\n\nMatrix of $S\\circ T$: {{matrix}}.\n\n$(S\\circ T)(\\mathbf x)=$ {{image}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["db87f1ff-64f3-5f26-a086-987dbad894cd" "8778d74d-fe75-58f6-a455-ae03ba73364f" "db6eae17-8bfe-54b8-80f3-1fb560588eec"]
  :question/worked-solution "Composition is read from right to left: $T$ acts first, so $A$ is the right-hand matrix in $BA$. Check the result by evaluating $T(\\mathbf x)$ and then $S(T(\\mathbf x))$ separately."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
