 {:db/id "ab610f7b-2f7f-5059-a1d6-09cd6f38b97a"
  :question/id #uuid "ab610f7b-2f7f-5059-a1d6-09cd6f38b97a"
  :question/problem "Source question: Assignment item (6); Kuttler 2017A, Exercise 5.3.5, printed p. 286 (PDF p. 298).\n\nLet $T$ be the linear transformation induced by\n$$A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\\\5&2\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nFind the matrix of $T^{-1}$. Show supporting work.\n\nMatrix of $T^{-1}$: {{matrix}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["b7ae50b7-29c9-557e-bed3-85ccc8ccee06" "94ac540d-5472-5358-bedd-274dfe89e154"]
  :question/worked-solution "The matrix of the inverse transformation is the inverse matrix. Check the determinant before using the $2\\times2$ inverse formula, and distribute its negative reciprocal to every entry."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
