 {:db/id "386c50c3-709b-5213-a1b5-ccc8d909870a"
  :answer/id #uuid "386c50c3-709b-5213-a1b5-ccc8d909870a"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "Using the standard positive (counterclockwise) rotation convention,\n$$R=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\pi/3)&-\\sin(2\\pi/3)\\\\\\sin(2\\pi/3)&\\cos(2\\pi/3)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac12&-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}&-\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nReflection across the $x$ axis has matrix $F=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}$. Since rotation occurs first, the required matrix is\n$$FR=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac12&-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}&\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nFor a check, $e_1$ rotates to $(-1/2,\\sqrt3/2)^T$, then reflects to $(-1/2,-\\sqrt3/2)^T$, the first column. The second column follows from $e_2$ in the same way."
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
