 {:db/id "7e4d787a-bb35-555f-bf55-a770c964bfd1"
  :question/id #uuid "7e4d787a-bb35-555f-bf55-a770c964bfd1"
  :question/problem "Source question: Assignment item (8), handout p. 1.\n\nLet $S$ and $T$ be linear transformations from $\\mathbb R^n$ to $\\mathbb R^n$, and let $\\{\\mathbf v_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf v_n\\}$ be a basis for $\\mathbb R^n$. Suppose $S(\\mathbf v_i)=T(\\mathbf v_i)$ for all $i=1,\\ldots,n$. Show that $S=T$. (This says that a linear transformation is determined by a basis!)"
  :question/answer-fields ["54b9db46-6b90-5678-9e8e-0d44dac9d729"]
  :question/worked-solution "Start with an arbitrary vector and expand it in the given basis. Apply linearity to both maps and use the hypothesis term by term. Agreement on the basis must be extended to every input before concluding that the functions are equal."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
